As of a few minutes ago, I received the eleventh request for a
reposting of Frank Crow's image generation software, developed at Ohio
State University.  This makes a critical mass of interest for reposting
the first version of the package.

I have not done any further modifications to the code, although Julian
Gomez, at OSU, says that a second version is available and is in the
public domain.

It would probably be best to post the most current version of the
software.  Unfortunately, I don't have the second version of the
software, but would be willing to post it if I did.  If someone posts
the second version, great.  I'd like a copy, too.  Otherwise, I'll
repost the first version in October.

